{"id":"word:hebrew:H1706","type":"word","title":"דְּבַשׁ","subtitle":"H1706 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"honey (from its stickiness ); by analogy, syrup","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to דְּבַשׁ (H1706) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 54 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"דְּבַשׁ (dᵉbash) means honey (from its stickiness ); by analogy, syrup First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 14 3."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"דְּבַשׁ","transliteration":"dᵉbash","pronunciation":"deb-ash'","strong":"H1706","lemmaId":"hebrew:H1706","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["וּ/דְבָֽשׁ","וּ/דְבַ֔שׁ","וּ/דְבָ֑שׁ","דְּבַ֣שׁ","וּ/דְבַשׁ֙"],"morphs":[["HC/Ncmsa",31],["HNcmsa",14],["HR/Ncmsa",5],["HTd/Ncmsa",2],["HNcmsc",1],["HNcmsc/Sp1cs",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"honey (from its stickiness ); by analogy, syrup","usage":"honey(-comb).","full":"H1706. debash דְּבַשׁ 54 noun masculine 1Sam 14:29 honey (named from colour according to Fl NHWB i. 430 ; Arabic () date-honey ; Late Hebrew דְּבַשׁ , Aramaic דּובשא , , , honey both of fruits and of bees; compare also Assyrian dišpu COT Gloss Zim BP 84 Dl Pr 70 ) — absolute ׳ד Gen 43:11 33 t.; דְּבָ֑שׁ Exod 3:8 18 t.; suffix דִּבְשִׁי Song 5:1 ; &#8212; honey , product of bees, used as food Judg 14:8-9 , 18 (in lion's carcass); found in (clefts of) rock Deut 32:13 ( ׳ד מִסֶּלַע , in song, J E), Psalm 81:17 ( ד ׳מִצּוּר ); in woods, on ground 1Sam 14:25 ( השׂדה עלפֿני ) 14:26 ( ד ׳הֵלֶךְ ; but read rather דְּבֹרוֺ הָלַךְ its bees had departed , We Dr after ᵐ5 ) 14:29 ; 14:43 ; transported in jar or bottle ד ׳בַּקְבֻּק 1Kin 14:3 ; contribution to priests and Levites 2Chr 31:5 ; || חֶמְאָה 2Sam 17:29 ; Isa 7:15 , 22 (in last two the being limited to such food is apparently token of destitution); kept in store Jer 41:8 ; a choice gift Gen 43:11 (J); article of trade Ezek 27:17 (in these two perhaps = grape syrup , modern dibs , compare Di Gen 43:11 see Rob BR ii. 81 ); forbidden as burnt offering Lev 2:11 (|| שְׂאֹר ); honey comb = הַדּ ׳יַעְרַת 1Sam 14:27 (compare יַעְרִי Song 5:1 ); also ד ׳צוּף Prov 16:24 (compare צופים נֹפֶת Psa 19:11 ); most often in phrase describing abundance in land of Canaan וּד חָלָב זָבַת ׳אֶרֶץ Exod 3:8 , 17 ; 13:5 ; 33:3 (all J E) Lev 20:24 (H) Num 13:27 ; 14:8 ; 16:18 , 14 (all J E) Deut 6:3 ; 11:9 ; 26:9 , 15 ; 27:3 ; 31:20 (all D) Josh 5:6 (D) Jer 11:5 ; 32:22 ; Ezek 20:6 , 15 ; compare Deut 8:8 ; 2Kin 18:32 (of land of captivity, words of the Rabshak); see also Ezek 16:13 , 19 ; Job 20:17 ד ׳נַחֲלֵי וְחֶמְאָה ; honey , used to illustrate moral teachings Prov 24:13 (|| נֹפֶת ), 25:16 , 27 (danger of surfeit); simile of sweetness of taste Ezek 3:3 (the roll), compare ׳בִּד כְּצַמִּיחִת Exod 16:31 (P; description of manna); of sweetness of the law Psa 19:11 (|| צוּפִים נֹפֶת ) compare 119:103 ; (of pleasant words Prov 16:24 compare above); sweetness of lips ׳ד וְחָלָב Song 4:11 ; figurative of love דִּבְשִׁי 5:1 (|| חֲלָבִי יֵינִי, יַעְרִי, ).","rootNote":"from an unused root meaning to be gummy ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 14 3","keyReferences":["1Kgs 14 3","1Sam 14 25","1Sam 14 26","1Sam 14 27","1Sam 14 29","1Sam 14 43","2Chr 31 5","2Kgs 18 32"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":54,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 14 3","book":"1Kgs","chapter":14,"verse":3,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"דְּבַ֖שׁ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 14 25","book":"1Sam","chapter":14,"verse":25,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"דְבַ֖שׁ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 14 26","book":"1Sam","chapter":14,"verse":26,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"דְּבָ֑שׁ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 14 27","book":"1Sam","chapter":14,"verse":27,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/דְּ